// Generated by .for-lewis/tools/player-scan/makeBuildData.ts from each Game-Maker build's stock
// player (its most common copy among the 1990s games); hand edits are lost on the next run.
// Per build: size, MD5 with the owner field zeroed, that owner field (a buyer's stamp in 2.x, an
// encoded registration field in 1.x; never kept), the "Version x.xx" line's offset (26 bytes
// before "Recreational Software Designs"), the About page's string slots, where XFERPLAY 3.00's
// text patches ([offset, length], plus the build's own stock text when it isn't 3.00's) and file extensions (each ".ext") sit in an older build, and a
// 16-bit CRC-32 of every 128-byte block, base64, so an import can tell which blocks an author
// changed without the stock .EXE. None of the players' bytes are here.

